# The Rust library is not built with -Zsanitizer=thread, so TSan cannot see
# the core's parking_lot mutex, std's channels or any of their atomics. All
# it sees of the library are the malloc, free and memcpy calls it intercepts,
# and with the ordering invisible each of them looks like a race: image
# pixels built whole and then published under the core lock
# (crates/scull-ffi/src/frame.rs), configuration views handed over through
# std's mpmc channel. Interceptors called from the library are ignored; the
# C side's own accesses stay checked.
called_from_lib:libscull_ffi
